WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:02.550
- [Narrator] Overwhelmed hospitals,

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:03.810
people dying on the streets

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.290
from lack of oxygen and
packed crematoriums.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.090
This is a snapshot of the
COVID-19 crisis in India.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.060
In contrast, just a few months ago

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.890
the prime minister declared
victory against the pandemic.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.807
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.045
After that, there were political rallies.

00:00:31.045 --> 00:00:32.920
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.750
Mass gatherings and religious
festivals like this one.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.350
And then on April 21st,
the country reported

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.830
a record number of COVID-19
cases in a single day.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:45.280
And those numbers kept
growing for several weeks.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.360
With many health experts
saying real numbers

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.950
are likely much higher.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.080
By May 7th, deaths soared past 4,000.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.450
As COVID cases in
several Western countries

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.170
have trended lower, the
scale of infection in India

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.940
and a new variant fresh reported there

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.490
have alarmed the rest of the world.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.120
- If you have a huge country like India,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.730
that's deep in its own COVID crisis right?

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:10.200
That means the pandemic is
not gonna end for the world.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.390
- [Narrator] Here's how India became

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:13.020
the world's COVID hotspot

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.363
and what that means for
the global pandemic.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.760
First, we have to go back to early 2020.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.420
As much of the world was
struggling to contain the virus,

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.323
India appeared to have things
under relative control.

00:01:27.185 --> 00:01:31.185
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:37.978 --> 00:01:40.630
Early on, Modi announced
the world's largest lockdown

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:43.690
in the country of 1.3 billion people.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.590
- He publicly came out multiple times

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.160
and said we have to pull it together,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.430
we have to wear masks, we
have to socially distance,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.900
there was a lot of respect
for COVID restrictions

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.746
and people were also scared.

00:01:54.746 --> 00:01:56.590
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.460
- [Narrator] The measures triggered

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.860
a mass migration of workers

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.800
trying to get back home from cities.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.860
Epidemiologist warned that this movement

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.240
of people could help
spread the virus undetected

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.740
to other parts of the country.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.410
But the number of reported COVID-19 cases

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.600
remained relatively low,
and India's apparent success

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.150
stood in contrast to some other
countries including the US

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.410
which was reporting more
cases than any other nation.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.910
Some public health experts
said a possible reason

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.680
for few cases in India could have been

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.760
the lack of widespread testing.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.290
But they also noted that the majority

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.470
of the population is under 25.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.780
And since asymptomatic
cases are more common

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.660
among young people, many
may have gone undetected.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.790
After a 10 week lockdown India
started to ease restrictions

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.810
and the number of cases started growing

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:43.870
with the first peak in September.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.170
- [Shan] It was quite bad
and the healthcare system

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:51.410
was stressed but the hospitals
didn't crumble or buckle.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:54.000
And we saw that actually in
other parts of the world,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.400
it was much worse.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.700
- [Narrator] Despite that first surge,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.240
by December India's numbers

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.210
had gone back down and by early 2021

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.310
life looked like it
was returning to normal

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.980
- [Shan] Stores were back
open, they were super packed,

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.490
restaurants were open filled
with people, indoor dining,

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:14.530
there were cricket matches
again, packed stadiums.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.880
Life in Delhi felt like another universe.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.860
The US was dealing with another wave,

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.470
right in December, January

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.820
- [Narrator] India was doing very well

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.740
compared to the US or the UK.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.040
And that's when Modi talked
of the country success

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.470
in front of other global leaders

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:29.936
at the world economic forum.

00:03:29.936 --> 00:03:33.853
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.203
So what went wrong?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.970
Public health experts blame
India's ferocious surge

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.360
on a combination of new factors.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.680
The first one, people became more relaxed

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.750
about COVID safety measures.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.420
Many people stopped wearing masks,

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.240
and there were several crowded gatherings

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.840
which public health experts say

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.510
may have been super spreader events

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.456
including huge political rallies.

00:03:56.456 --> 00:04:00.373
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.310
April was a key election
month and political parties

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.140
including Modi's BJP
party organized events

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.530
across the West Bangor state.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.660
A BJP spokesperson said
that no one had anticipated

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.180
the magnitude of the COVID-19 surge,

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.450
adding that Modi and
other members of his party

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:21.020
followed all the safety
protocols in place at the time.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.390
Right around then, resources
to fight the pandemic

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.840
weren't reinforced or maintained.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.130
- Everyone essentially
thought that COVID was over

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.480
by January hospitals were taking
down their COVID-19 wards,

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.360
testing centers that had
been started last year

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.130
were also being dismantled.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.810
It's only oxygen plants

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:43.410
where they had allocated
the budget were never built.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.650
- [Narrator] And on top of all of this

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.420
highly contagious variants
that were first identified

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.930
in the UK and South Africa were
circulating in the country.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.050
As well as a new variant known as B.1.617

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:56.170
that originated in India

00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:00.040
- The 617 in India,
it's a wildly opponent.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.500
- [Narrator] The WHO has
said preliminary studies

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.830
indicate that this one
may be more contagious

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.140
than some other variants.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:09.270
And has since been detected
in more than 40 countries

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:12.460
including the US, UK and France.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.660
This has added urgency to
the global vaccination race,

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.660
which has so far helped cases plummet

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.460
in some of those countries.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.040
So, even as the COVID
situation has improved

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.700
in some parts of the West,

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.860
the fight against the
pandemic across the globe

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.130
is far from over.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:31.160
- A big lesson is just
countries can't get complacent.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.820
And even if one country is doing well

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.480
if another country is not
doing well in terms of COVID

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.928
that will affect every other
country in the world too.

00:05:39.928 --> 00:05:42.511
(upbeat music)

